Correction: the description claimed there was no way to suppress the id. There is, and it is the usual one for any attribute: `attr: {id: false}` renders no `id` at all, because the `attributes` block skips a value that `is same as(false)`. Verified through the real rendering path:

```
attr.id = false => <form name="form" method="get" >
attr.id = ''    => <form name="form" method="get" id="">
attr.id = null  => <form name="form" method="get" id="">
```

So no new opt-out is needed. Making `''` mean "remove" would special-case `id`, since `attr: {class: ''}` would still render `class=""`, and it would silently change what that value does today. The description and the `UPGRADE-8.2.md` entry now both mention `attr: {id: false}`.

